e against what changed.\n\n**Left for the judge, not edited:**\n- Both the use case and the REST adapter log when the provider is unavailable.\n- The use case checks the payment outcome twice.\n- `CancelPaymentAsync` answers \"refused\" for a cancellation the provider doesn't offer. Giving it its own outcome would change the port's contract, which is more than tidying.\n\n**Checks:**\n- **Build:** no errors.\n- **Unit:** 178 passed, 4 skipped.\n- **Integration:** 65 passed, 1 skipped.\n- **Architecture:** 129 passed.\n- **End-to-end:** 38 passed, 1 skipped.\n- **Format:** `dotnet format` found nothing to correct.\n\nNo test was changed. The profile names no tidy carrier, so the stage ran here, and I applied `dca-discipline`; the only file written this round was `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/tidy.md`. No other stage was run.","ttft_ms":2660,"type":"result","duration_ms":129759,"uuid":"f0a4d471-a679-439b-b3d1-4201e77383e4","ttft_stream_ms":1763,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":1763,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
